# HEX ONLY (read-safe). Decodes to the SAFE tui-showcase: an HONEST, self-labeling,
# DISPLAY-ONLY educational board. Cat'd in a traditional terminal it paints a full-screen
# "WHAT YOU SEE vs WHAT IS THERE" table where every row NAMES a text-attack class and
# shows a LIVE example, so plain cat hides the trick and a safe tool reveals it. It
# changes only the DISPLAY: the window title (OSC 0) and the alternate screen (?1049h),
# both undone by `reset`. It does NOT touch the clipboard, type at the prompt, or run
# anything: the notification (OSC 9), clipboard (OSC 52) and output->input (DSR) rows are
# SHOWN as inert readable text, never fired -- those classes are fired + conformance-
# tested live in the SANDBOX by their own PoCs (notification-spoof, osc52-clipboard-write,
# device-status-reflection), and the RCE reflection variant is described only, sandbox-
# tested. Live display classes here: homoglyph (Cyrillic + Greek), ASCII look-alike,
# bidi (U+202E), zero-width (U+200B), BOM (U+FEFF), combining/Zalgo, fullwidth (U+FF2x),
# control-byte CR+erase, hidden-by-colour (SGR), DEC charset shift, OSC 8 hyperlink,
# OSC 0 title, CSI ?1049h alt-screen, and honest Greek as the NON-attack contrast.
# Viewing THIS hex never fires anything (SAFETY.md); run the decoded file only in a
# throwaway terminal and 'reset' after.
